# Branch test audit: correction tasklist

## Scope and evidence

- Purpose: an implementation contract for maintainers correcting test responsibility, placement, and confirmed defects. This document does not implement those corrections.
- Audited branch: `crafting-menu`, at `95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914`.
- Comparison: `origin/master...HEAD`; merge base `ce97c109caa953085666ad09a797bf49fe81b430`.
- Scope: all 330 test methods in 23 new files, the two added configuration methods, their fixtures, and the changed test-project configuration. Theory rows are additional executions, not additional methods.
- Review: configured `test_reviewer`, using the test-workflow review guidance and actual boundaries rather than folder names.
- Same-reviewer reconciliation assigned all 332 methods once: 123 Unit, 141 Component, 68 Integration, and zero E2E. No test deletion, duplication, or method splitting is required by this disposition.
- Behavioral reference: [Recipe Book design](RecipeBook.md). Existing implementation is evidence, not permission to strengthen its public contract.
- Preserve all existing behavior and unrelated work. Do not remove meaningful coverage merely because it is misclassified or shares a large file.
- Source line references below describe the audited revision. Original-suite links point to that pinned revision; use the ledger's placements and method identities for migrated suites.

### Confirmed findings

| ID | Priority | Discrepancy | Correction phases |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| F1 | High | Windows-only asset paths in lifecycle and shader tests contradict the supported Ubuntu test configuration. | 2, 6 |
| F2a | Medium | Filter intersection test requires registration-order short-circuiting excluded by the contract. | 2 |
| F2b | Medium | Atomic-publication test injects failure by numbered predicate invocation rather than semantic scenario. | 2 |
| F3 | Medium | Session allocation-reuse test hardcodes allocator-internal native-validation counts. | 2 |
| F4 | Medium | Exact GLSL substring/order checks freeze syntax without proving compilation or rendered behavior. | 5 |
| F5 | Low | Complex added tests lack clear setup/action/assertion phase delineation. | 4 |
| C1 | Organization | Unit/E2E folders and traits misdescribe component and native-integration boundaries. | 1, 3, 6 |
| O1 | Organization | Mixed subjects, levels, and fixture ownership put tests in unrelated files. | 1, 3, 4 |
| O2 | Low | Test project adds an identical second managed `cairo-sharp` reference. | 2 |

### Verification already obtained

- A focused Windows run built successfully: 39 passed, zero failed, zero skipped.
- Selector: `FullyQualifiedName~CraftingNativeTransferTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeFilterSetTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookToggle_|FullyQualifiedName~ShaderSourceRetainsApprovedPaletteOutlineAndSeparateCornerGeometry|FullyQualifiedName~ExplicitBookOpeningFocusesSearchAndAcceptsTheFirstCharacter`.
- Command shape: `dotnet test .\VanillaExpanded.Tests\VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter "<selector above>" --verbosity minimal`.
- Compilation/analyzer warnings were present. This is not a warning-free-build claim.
- Remaining methods were reviewed statically, not executed.
- No Linux run, live multiplayer workflow, GPU compilation/rendering, or in-game visual acceptance was performed.

## Phase 1 - Establish the placement and discovery contract

Dependencies: none.

Implementation assets:
- [Pinned method ledger](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestAudit/recipebook-baseline.jsonl): the first JSONL record defines source/placement identifiers and row fields; the following 332 rows retain original identities, categories, fixtures, collections, and theory data separately from planned placements. Fixture references use bare names for direct dependencies and `helper:Method()->Fixture` for dependencies created through helpers.
- [Category contract](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestCategories.cs): the trait key is `Category`; values match the `Unit`, `Component`, `Integration`, and `E2E` directory names. Phase 1 reserved the Component and Integration locations and recorded each method's target category; Phase 3 applies those placements.
- [Shared GUI support](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/Gui/GuiRenderFixture.cs) owns the common native GUI collection and client/render/texture fixture outside a test suite. [Recipe Book rendering support](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/RecipeBook/RecipeBookRenderFixture.cs) adds feature-owned cache, atlas, shader, and bake lifetimes; [Recipe Book dialog support](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/RecipeBook/RecipeBookTestFixtures.cs) owns shared dialog/session helpers.
- Preserve the `Recipe book native GUI` collection's disabled parallelization across all consumers and retain global/configuration/language restoration and resource disposal. Placement changes must not create another collection definition.
- Completion evidence: the eight affected suites passed 578 tests with zero failures or skips. The second review and independent completion audit accepted the phase after helper-resolved fixture metadata corrections; the ledger retains 332 unique methods and the 123/141/68 planned placement totals.

- [x] P1.1 Capture a method-level baseline for all 332 introduced methods, including original fully qualified identity, theory data, category, fixture, collection, and actual tested boundary.
  - [x] Keep the existing configuration methods outside this branch's additions out of remediation unless fixture extraction directly requires compatibility work.
  - [x] Use the complete reviewed-file inventory below to ensure no added suite is omitted.
- [x] P1.2 Establish `Unit`, `Component`, and `Integration` directories and matching category traits within the existing test project.
  - [x] Unit: an isolated rule/subject; real data objects alone do not automatically make a test component-level.
  - [x] Component: composed production collaborators exercised behind mocked external services.
  - [x] Integration: a real native/engine boundary or compatibility contract.
  - [x] Reserve E2E for a complete externally driven workflow. The seven current native-transfer tests do not qualify.
  - [x] Do not migrate to a separate test assembly merely to obtain an Integration folder; first preserve internal access, fixtures, and discovery.
- [x] P1.3 Assign each method exactly one primary responsibility, destination, and level before moving mixed suites.
  - [x] Follow the responsibility matrix below, including narrow unit cases that must not move wholesale with a mixed file.
  - [x] Preserve coherent multi-transition lifecycle scenarios when they test one responsibility.
  - [x] Record any further split needed to distinguish a pure rule from its native compatibility coverage.
- [x] P1.4 Identify shared fixture ownership and serialization requirements.
  - [x] Extract `RecipeBookRenderFixture` from the renderer-test file to feature-neutral support when shared GUI tests use it.
  - [x] Extract common dialog/session fixtures from catch-all suites only where multiple focused suites need them.
  - [x] Preserve engine-global restoration, disposal, and collection-based serialization.

Exit criteria:
- [x] Every introduced method has one destination; no method is unassigned or duplicated.
- [x] Destination names express production responsibility, not the feature that happened to introduce the test.
- [x] The discovery and serialization contract is explicit before extraction.

## Phase 2 - Correct known test defects without changing feature behavior

Dependencies: Phase 1, so corrected methods retain traceable identities during extraction.

Completion evidence: the four affected suites passed 386 tests with zero failures or skips on Windows; 34 existing compiler/analyzer warnings remain. The second review and independent completion audit accepted P2.1-P2.5. Linux execution remains deferred to Phase 6.

- [x] P2.1 Fix portable asset lookup (F1).
  - [x] Replace the three lifecycle fixture asset paths, originally at lines 3672-3685 in [RecipeBookLifecycleTests.cs](https://github.com/dsisco11/VanillaExpanded/blob/95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914/VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookLifecycleTests.cs) and extracted in Phase 1 to [RecipeBookTestFixtures.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/RecipeBook/RecipeBookTestFixtures.cs).
  - [x] Replace the shader asset path at original lines 924-927 in [RecipeBookIconRendererTests.cs](https://github.com/dsisco11/VanillaExpanded/blob/95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914/VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookIconRendererTests.cs).
  - [x] Use platform-portable path segments or deliberately copied test assets; changing only the working directory is insufficient.
  - [x] Fail explicitly for missing assets rather than skipping or returning successful defaults.
- [x] P2.2 Correct filter-contract overconstraint (F2a).
  - [x] Rewrite `ProvidersReceiveTheExactEvaluatedSelectionAndMayShortCircuit`, original lines 73-88 in [RecipeFilterSetTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeFilterSetTests.cs).
  - [x] Preserve exact evaluated-selection identity and intersection-result assertions.
  - [x] Make providers independently evaluable; do not make a later provider throw solely to enforce registration order or short-circuiting.
- [x] P2.3 Correct atomic-publication failure injection (F2b).
  - [x] Rewrite `FailureWhileFilteringStableRecipesDoesNotPublishPartialRows`, original lines 498-520 in [RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs](https://github.com/dsisco11/VanillaExpanded/blob/95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914/VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs).
  - [x] Fail for a semantically identifiable selection/scenario, not the second predicate call.
  - [x] Preserve assertions that published rows remain unchanged, no premature notification occurs, and a subsequent valid operation recovers.
  - [x] Do not require invocation counts that the filtering contract explicitly excludes.
- [x] P2.4 Decouple session reuse from allocator validation protocol (F3).
  - [x] Correct `CriteriaChangesReuseAllocationsAndInventoryRefreshEvaluatesExactlyOnce`, original lines 192-233 in [RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs](https://github.com/dsisco11/VanillaExpanded/blob/95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914/VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs).
  - [x] Retain capture counts and allocation-identity evidence.
  - [x] Compare criteria-change validation work against a recorded baseline rather than hardcoding native callback totals of two and four.
  - [x] Keep any justified ordinary/shift native-validation protocol assertions in allocator/native-validation suites, not session reuse tests.
- [x] P2.5 Remove the duplicate managed Cairo reference (O2).
  - [x] Remove only the identical duplicate at original lines 83-86 in [VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj); preserve the existing reference and native library copying.

Exit criteria:
- [x] Corrected tests enforce behavioral contracts rather than incidental iteration/validation implementation.
- [x] No assertion strength is lost merely to make tests pass.
- [x] Portable asset lookup is ready for actual Windows and Linux execution in Phase 6.

## Phase 3 - Move and split tests by responsibility and boundary

Dependencies: Phases 1 and 2.

Completion evidence: all 332 methods occupy their 69 mapped suites with bodies and theory data preserved: 123 Unit, 141 Component, and 68 Integration. Focused verification passed 833 tests; the full test project passed 2,789, with zero failures or skips. The build reported 29 warnings. The second review and independent completion audit accepted the migration and its documented collection reconciliation.

The following deterministic mapping supersedes broad file-level classifications. Source selectors refer to attributed test-method declaration lines at `95a3d284`, inclusive, not slices of method bodies. They exclude helpers, constructors, and disposal methods. Move complete methods with every theory-data attribute. Each method belongs to one row only.

Destination files are within the existing test project at `{Level}/{Feature}/{Destination}.cs`. Use `RecipeBook` as the feature unless the row names `Gui/` or `Configuration/`. An unchanged destination name retains the responsibility, not an incorrect original directory. These destinations now identify the migrated suites; source selectors remain historical.

