## Phase 4 - Clarify test phases and fixture ownership

Dependencies: Phase 3.

Implementation evidence:
- Generic GUI consumers use [GuiRenderFixture](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/Gui/GuiRenderFixture.cs); [RecipeBookRenderFixture](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/TestSupport/RecipeBook/RecipeBookRenderFixture.cs) adds Recipe Book composition and disposes its cache before restoring shared engine globals.
- Inventory reconciliation retains every original method exactly once in its Phase 3 destination: 332 methods across 69 suites (123 Unit, 141 Component, 68 Integration). No Phase 4 method moves, splits, or replacements were needed. All 129 theories retain their data, including the 40-entry MemberData provider and its recorded hash; the immutable ledger remains unchanged.
- Separate full-project verification passed 2,789 tests with zero failures or skips; the build retained 29 existing warnings. The original 176 serialized GUI methods plus the approved ownership-test addition remain in the single disabled-parallelization GUI collection.
- The second review and fresh independent completion audit accepted the phase with no required issues or evidence gaps. Linux, GPU, and live-runtime acceptance remain outside this phase.

- [x] P4.1 Add necessary Arrange/Act/Assert phase delineation to complex reviewed additions (F5).
  - [x] Make setup, interactions, and expectations clear in long multi-transition tests.
  - [x] Retain coherent lifecycle scenarios rather than mechanically splitting them to obtain a single assertion block.
  - [x] Respect the project rule against unnecessary comments. The review reference literally requires AAA comments without a simple-test exception, but that is not an established project requirement for filler comments. Record this policy reconciliation rather than treating clear simple tests as behavioral defects.
  - [x] Clarify evaluation/projection/refresh boundaries in `CriteriaChangesReuseAllocationsAndInventoryRefreshEvaluatesExactlyOnce` and prior-publication/failure/recovery boundaries in `FailureWhileFilteringStableRecipesDoesNotPublishPartialRows`.
  - [x] Clarify old press/rebinding/new press in `HeldReleaseCannotActivateReboundTileAndRequiresNewPress`, and editing/clear/resize/reopen in `InlineSearchClearUsesNativeEditingAndPreservesOtherCriteriaAcrossResizeAndReopen`.
  - [x] Clarify old-composition capture before scale mutation in `ScaleTransitionCapturesTheOldCompositionRowBeforeRestoringAtTheNewScale`.
  - [x] Clarify mid-world enable/disable versus reload in `DisabledAtWorldLoadDoesNotLoadSystemAndEnablingWaitsForReload` and `DisablingLiveDisposesSystemAndBlocksReactivationUntilReload`.
  - [x] Distinguish inventory reopen from composer replacement in `BrowsingStateSurvivesInventoryReopeningAndComposerReplacement`.
  - [x] Distinguish old/new request generations in `ReloadedDeferredCompletionsDoNotUnblockTheNewFourRequestBatch`, and submission failure/retry in `NativeSubmissionFailurePropagatesWithoutTouchingGuiStateAndCanRetry`.
  - [x] Clarify capture/cancellation/resource reuse in `ScrollbarPointerFeedbackTracksCaptureAndCancelsWithoutExtraScrollOrUploads`, and clipped input/scrolling/keyboard restoration in `ClippedTabsRejectPointerActivationAndKeyboardWrapRestoresAccessAfterMovement`.
  - [x] Distinguish accepted movement from interrupted unsent work in `CompetingUpdateAfterFirstPacketStopsUnsentWorkAndKeepsAcceptedMove`, and local dispatch from authoritative updates in `NativeSynchronizationRefreshesCurrentInventoryWithoutClassifyingServerOutcomes`.
- [x] P4.2 Ensure extracted fixtures have clear ownership, complete cleanup, and a focused public testing vocabulary.
  - [x] Preserve native texture/composer disposal, engine-global restoration, and existing GUI serialization.
  - [x] Reuse existing support rather than cloning fixture implementations into each new suite.
  - [x] Keep feature-specific composition helpers out of generic shared-GUI support.
- [x] P4.3 Reconcile the original method inventory with the final suites before verification.
  - [x] Identify every retained, moved, split, or deliberately replaced method.
  - [x] Preserve theory cases and failure-path assertions, not just aggregate method counts.

Exit criteria:
- [x] Test flow and fixture responsibility are understandable without navigating unrelated test suites.
- [x] No cleanup, isolation, or coverage is lost through extraction.

## Phase 5 - Make shader evidence truthful and behavioral

Dependencies: Phase 3's renderer/cache/asset split and Phase 2's portable asset lookup.

- [ ] P5.1 Replace the overclaimed source-syntax mechanism in `ShaderSourceRetainsApprovedPaletteOutlineAndSeparateCornerGeometry` (F4), now in [RecipeBookShaderAssetTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookShaderAssetTests.cs), originally at lines 924-945 in the pinned renderer suite.
  - [ ] Retain approved palette values and geometry dimensions as legitimate requirements.
  - [ ] Remove dependence on exact expression spelling and textual ordering where equivalent shader behavior is allowed.
  - [ ] Keep any useful source/asset check explicitly labelled as a limited structural guard, not proof of compilation or rendered appearance.
  - [ ] Preserve mocked renderer protocol/state tests; their responsibility is submission and state management, not GPU behavior.
- [ ] P5.2 Establish actual compiled/rendered evidence for palette, availability outlines, and separate selection-corner geometry where a suitable environment is available.
  - [ ] Confirm meaningful changes to those outcomes are detected and behavior-preserving source refactoring does not fail merely for syntax.
  - [ ] If GPU/in-game validation is unavailable, record the exact remaining acceptance gap and keep that validation item open. Do not silently substitute substring checks or a mocked compile result.

Exit criteria:
- [ ] Asset guards and renderer mocks no longer imply GPU coverage they do not supply.
- [ ] Actual visual validation has evidence, or its incompleteness remains explicit and unchecked.

## Phase 6 - Verify discovery, portability, behavior, and documentation

Dependencies: Phases 2-5. Unavailable environment-dependent acceptance stays open rather than being marked complete.

- [ ] P6.1 Build and run the focused changed suites using the repository's existing test runner.
  - [ ] First run the affected responsibilities together; expand to the full project after the extraction changes discovery/fixtures broadly.
  - [ ] Run category-filtered discovery/execution for Unit, Component, and Integration and compare with P1's method-level map.
  - [ ] Confirm each mapped method is discovered exactly once at its intended level; verify any retained E2E category contains genuine E2E workflows.
  - [ ] Preserve and investigate failures rather than masking them with skips, broad catches, or successful defaults.
- [ ] P6.2 Execute affected asset-dependent suites on Windows and Linux.
  - [ ] Verify all three lifecycle asset locations and the shader location are read successfully on both platforms.
  - [ ] Preserve the existing unfiltered Ubuntu CI test run; do not claim classification alone caused CI omissions.
  - [ ] Record commands, revision, passed/failed/skipped counts, warnings, and environment limitations.
- [ ] P6.3 Reconcile behavioral assertions after extraction.
  - [ ] Confirm filter failures still preserve published rows and recover without enforcing excluded invocation semantics.
  - [ ] Confirm criteria changes reuse allocations without binding session tests to allocator-internal validation counts.
  - [ ] Confirm native-transfer tests still exercise the real native compatibility boundary after reclassification.
  - [ ] Confirm global-state cleanup and collection serialization remain effective across the new suites.
- [ ] P6.4 Update directly related test documentation to match the implemented organization.
  - [ ] Update verification links and commands in [RecipeBook.md](RecipeBook.md).
  - [ ] Update testing conventions in [copilot-instructions.md](../.github/copilot-instructions.md) for Component/Integration locations and traits while preserving Unit/E2E guidance.
  - [ ] Remove misleading E2E or shader-proof claims wherever the moved suites are documented.
  - [ ] Clearly separate headless automation from GPU, live multiplayer, and in-game acceptance.
- [ ] P6.5 Obtain configured independent test review of the complete coherent correction batch.
  - [ ] Reconcile every confirmed finding F1-F5, C1, O1, and O2 against this tasklist and final evidence.
  - [ ] Resolve new issues caused by the moves without expanding into unrelated pre-existing test debt.
  - [ ] Close all correction tasks only when their evidence is recorded; leave unavailable visual/runtime acceptance explicitly open.

